{%- comment -%}
  The product page's rail block — title, price, size and add-to-cart, per
  turn 8b. The images then take the whole field, which is the point: the buy
  controls are always on screen in the rail, so the photography never has to
  share the fold with them.

  IT DOES NOT OWN ANY STATE. There is exactly one product form on the page —
  Dawn's, in main-product — and this block drives it:

    • the size buttons click the real radio in <variant-selects>, which is
      precisely what a visitor clicking the on-page picker does, so Dawn
      updates the variant, the price and availability by its own code path;
    • Add to cart calls requestSubmit() on that same form, so the cart drawer
      and notification behave exactly as a native add;
    • the price here is re-read from the page after each change.

  This is the mechanism sticky-atc already uses in production. A second form,
  or a second copy of the variant state, is how a buy button ends up adding
  the wrong variant.

  The primary nav is deliberately absent on this template — 8b replaces it
  with "← Shop" and the buy block. The wordmark above still goes home.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign v = product.selected_or_first_available_variant

  comment
    The size axis. Named options win; otherwise the first option is it, which
    is right for a single-axis product and harmless for none.
  endcomment
  assign size_option = blank
  for option in product.options_with_values
    assign name_down = option.name | downcase
    if name_down contains 'size' and size_option == blank
      assign size_option = option
    endif
  endfor
  if size_option == blank and product.has_only_default_variant == false
    assign size_option = product.options_with_values.first
  endif
-%}

<a class="alp-rail__back" href="{{ collection.url | default: routes.all_products_collection_url }}">← Shop</a>

<div class="alp-rail__product">
  <p class="alp-rail__ptitle">{{ product.title | escape }}</p>
  <p class="alp-rail__pprice" data-alp-rp-price>
    {{- v.price | money }} {{ cart.currency.iso_code -}}
  </p>
</div>

{%- if size_option != blank -%}
  <div class="alp-rail__sizes">
    <p class="alp-rail__eyebrow">{{ size_option.name | escape }}</p>
    <div class="alp-rail__sizerow" data-alp-rp-options data-alp-rp-position="{{ size_option.position }}">
      {%- for value in size_option.values -%}
        <button
          class="alp-rail__size{% if value == size_option.selected_value %} is-on{% endif %}"
          type="button"
          data-alp-rp-value="{{ value | escape }}"
          {% if value == size_option.selected_value %}aria-current="true"{% endif %}
        >{{ value | escape }}</button>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

<button class="alp-chip alp-rail__atc" type="button" data-alp-rp-submit>
  {%- if v.available -%}Add to cart{%- else -%}Sold out{%- endif -%}
</button>
